  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of what these files establish for the impact report:\n\n**Log4j2 bridge module structure (rel_2.20.0):**\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml` \u2014 the Log4j2-API\u2192SLF4J adapter (used when app code calls the Log4j2 API but you want SLF4J/Logback as the backend). Depends only on `log4j-api` + `slf4j-api`.\n- `log4j-slf4j-impl/pom.xml` and `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml` \u2014 the reverse direction (SLF4J\u2192Log4j2 Core), used when SLF4J calls should be routed into Log4j2. The 2.20.0 release note in `RELEASE-NOTES.md` documents LOG4J2-3601: *\"Add Log4j2 Core as default runtime dependency of the SLF4J2-to-Log4j2 API bridge\"* \u2014 `log4j-slf4j2-impl` now declares `log4j-core` at `<scope>runtime</scope>` directly, where earlier/adjacent bindings didn't guarantee that transitive pull.\n- `SLF4JServiceProvider.java` (slf4j2-impl) implements the SLF4J 2.x SPI (`org.slf4j.spi.SLF4JServiceProvider`), replacing the SLF4J 1.x `StaticLoggerBinder` mechanism (`log4j-slf4j-impl/src/main/java/org/slf4j/impl/StaticLoggerBinder.java`) \u2014 a structural/SPI-shape change between the two binding modules.\n\n**Spring Boot detection logic:**\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`'s inner `Factory` class detects Log4j2 availability via `ClassUtils.isPresent(\"org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory\", ...)` \u2014 a class that lives in **log4j-core**, not log4j-api or the bridge jars. This means detection is contingent on log4j-core actually landing on the classpath, which is exactly what the slf4j2-impl bridge restructuring changed (now guaranteed via its own runtime dependency, reinforced by `spring-boot-starter-log4j2` also declaring `log4j-core` directly as `api`).\n- `LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 base class, loads factories via `spring.factories` (`LoggingSystemFactory=Logback,...,Log4J2,...,Java`), ordered so Logback wins by default unless Log4j2 starter excludes it.\n- `spring-boot-starter-log4j2/build.gradle` confirms the dependency chain: `log4j-slf4j2-impl` + `log4j-core` + `log4j-jul`.\n\nThe dependency chain Spring Boot \u2192 SLF4J \u2192 Log4j2 is: app code / libraries call SLF4J \u2192 `log4j-slf4j2-impl`'s `SLF4JServiceProvider` binds SLF4J to Log4j2's `Log4jLoggerFactory` \u2192 Log4j2 Core (`Log4jContextFactory`) is the class Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` probes for to select Log4j2 as the active `LoggingSystem`.",
